    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Vijayalaya founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> in 848, and the Cholas held peninsular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tungabhadra-river">Tungabhadra River</a> as one state between 907 and 1215.</li><li>Rajendra I reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>, built a new capital called Gangaikonda Cholapuram, and in 1025 launched naval raids on the ports of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>.</li><li>The empire declined after Kulothunga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> III's defeat by Maravarman Sundara Pandiyan II in 1215–16 and ceased to exist by 1279, absorbed by the Pandyan empire.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>According to the Malay chronicle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-annals">Sejarah Melayu</a>, the rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> sultanate claimed descent from the kings of the Chola empire.</p></aside>
    </section>

